scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: jazz-legends
run_id: 3
total_caught: 2
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 10
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 27.0
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The config
    implementation uses deny_unknown_fields and loads TOML, but no evidence of distinguishing
    NotFound from parse/permission errors in the fallback path.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented sanitize_message() in error.rs Display impl for credential
    sanitization (CWE-209). Reviewer verified it but also noted NotFound and Config
    variants inconsistently skip sanitization (finding #7), so partial catch.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev implemented CRLF/null stripping in client.rs:16-19 (header injection
    prevention), but SiemClient.tenant_id still uses raw String rather than axiathon-core's
    validated TenantId type. The stripping mitigates CWE-113 but doesn't use the type-safe
    approach. No phase flagged the missing TenantId usage.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer noted version mismatches (dirs 5 vs 6, toml 0.8 vs 0.9) but did
    not flag that dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true.
    The core issue of version drift from not using workspace inheritance was not caught.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on ClientConfig (config.rs:11).
    Reviewer verified this in finding #11. Unknown TOML keys including token cause
    parse errors rather than silent acceptance.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in tests. TEA wrote 9 config_loading tests but the specific vacuous assertion
    was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via let _ = config. TEA wrote config tests but didn't flag this pattern.
